{
  "id": "0043s_lava",
  "title": "Cebar con lava",
  "caption": "¿Sabías que para cebar mate lo recomendable es agua y no lava del Kilauea? 🧉🌋\nSeguime para más datos de mate.",
  "hashtags": [
    "#mate",
    "#datoscuriosos",
    "#argentina",
    "#humor",
    "#sabiasque"
  ],
  "story": {
    "logline": "A \"did you know\" gag: mate is made with water, not with Kilauea lava; real numbers (1,150 °C, 15 times hotter, alpaca melts at 1,100 °C) and the result: no yerba, no bombilla, no tongue.",
    "facts": [
      "Kilauea lava erupts at about 1,150 °C (USGS).",
      "Mate water is best at 70–80 °C.",
      "1,150 / 75 ≈ 15.",
      "Alpaca (nickel silver) melts at about 1,100 °C."
    ],
    "places": {
      "casita": "the dollhouse kitchen on a lawn; a volcano far behind it with a lava river to the back wall"
    }
  },
  "cast": {
    "vos": "Tomás, about 25, short dark hair, light blue shirt, beige trousers"
  },
